# Committed on purpose. Vite reads this at build time for `npm run build`, so
# every Vercel deployment built from a commit picks it up automatically — no
# dashboard setting, no CLI flag, no state living outside the repo.
#
# SECURITY: VITE_-prefixed values are inlined into the public JavaScript bundle.
# Only put things here that are safe to publish. Secrets belong in the Vercel
# dashboard as non-VITE_ variables, never in this file.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DEMO MODE — remove this line to go live.
#
# While set, /book renders the built-in DemoCalendar (sample availability, an
# on-screen banner, nothing booked) instead of the Cal.com embed. The real
# per-doctor Cal.com event types in src/data/clinic.js do not exist yet.
#
# Going live is one commit:
#   1. Create the Cal.com event types (docs/BOOKING_SETUP.md)
#   2. Delete the line below
#   3. Flip public/robots.txt back to Allow
#   4. Commit and push
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_DEMO_BOOKING=1
